# Documentation

Keep code comments and JSDoc minimal. Prefer readable names and structure over narration.

## Where docs live

- **Key project knowledge** (architecture, build, product decisions, invariants) goes in `./context/` files.
- New `./context/` docs must **earn their place**: only add or expand when the knowledge is durable, non-obvious, and useful across sessions—not a dump of the last change.
- Prefer updating an existing context file over creating a new one when the topic already has a home.

## Inline docs

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — JSDoc that restates the signature
/** Adds a and b. @param a First number @param b Second number @returns Sum */
function add(a: number, b: number): number {
  return a + b;
}

// ✅ GOOD — no comment; the code is enough
function add(a: number, b: number): number {
  return a + b;
}

// ✅ GOOD — rare inline note for a non-obvious constraint
// Real returns are annualized; monthly inputs must be converted before use.
function applyRealReturn(balance: number, annualRate: number): number {
  // ...
}
```

- Do not add JSDoc, file headers, or comment blocks by default.
- Comment only when intent is easy to miss (workaround, invariant, subtle math).
- Do not duplicate `./context/` content into source files.
